            </note>
            <note corresp="#d47-f2" n="2" xml:id="d47-f2-content">
                <p>Eduardo Acosta.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d47-f3" n="3" xml:id="d47-f3-content">
                <p>Secretary Dulles spoke with the President at 4:01 p.m. that afternoon and
                    informed him of the results of his discussion with the Venezuelan Chargé.
                    Bernau’s transcript of this telephone conversation reads in part as follows:
                    “The Sec said he talked with the Chargé but he knows nothing and the Sec said he
                    spoke on the Pres’ behalf and his own to say we expected the Govt to do
                    everything possible to protect the VP of the US and his wife who were the
                    invited guests of the Venezuelan Govt and that if they did not have the will or
                    capacity to do so we would want to know it in a hurry to concert on further
                    measures on it.” (Eisenhower Library, Dulles Papers, White House Telephone
                    Conversations)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
